        "<b>Too hot</b>: vasodilation and sweating. <b>Too cold</b>: vasoconstriction and shivering. Hypothalamus integrates.",
        "<b>Fever</b> = raised set point (cytokines); <b>hyperthermia</b> = heat gain exceeds loss at normal set point.",
        "Heat-vulnerable groups: older adults, children, SCI above T6, MS, diuretics and anticholinergics.",
